Many of us, including me, thought it to be right. Later, I found an example
of such an use of 'mo' in the baselined grammar, Ch. 7, Sec. 9:

> 9.5)    lo mo prenu cu darxi do
>                 .i barda
>         A [what selbri?] type-of person hit you?
>                 (Observative:) A big thing.
>         Which person hit you?  The big one.

